IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `pid-dates`
IMPORT `pid-rules`
IMPORT `pid-seat`

-- Public Interest Disclosures Act 2012 (Vic) -- worked cases for the discloser's questions (pid-seat.l4), the date helpers
-- (pid-dates.l4) and the shared rules (pid-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text;
-- none was copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the
-- law. The facts are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

-- Short names for the entities and subjects.
`IBAC` MEANS `the IBAC`
`Ombudsman` MEANS `the Ombudsman`
`IOV` MEANS `Integrity Oversight Victoria`
`IOC` MEANS `the Integrity and Oversight Committee`
`Speaker` MEANS `the Speaker of the Legislative Assembly`
`President` MEANS `the President of the Legislative Council`
`VicPol` MEANS `Victoria Police`
`JC` MEANS `the Judicial Commission`
`CMI` MEANS `the Chief Municipal Inspector`
`PWSIC` MEANS `the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission`
`PSB` MEANS `a public service body`
`PPO` MEANS `a prescribed public officer`
`Council` MEANS `a Council`
`GW` MEANS `Gellung Warl`
`Chairs` MEANS `the Chairpersons of the First Peoples' Assembly, or a person named in Gellung Warl's procedures`
`elsewhere` MEANS `some other person or body`

`re IOV` MEANS `Integrity Oversight Victoria or an Integrity Oversight Victoria Officer`
`re IBAC` MEANS `the IBAC, an IBAC Officer or a Public Interest Monitor`
`re judge` MEANS `a judicial officer, or a member of VCAT who is not a judicial officer`
`re police` MEANS `a member of Victoria Police personnel other than the Chief Commissioner`
`re InfoComm` MEANS `the Information Commissioner or the Health Complaints Commissioner`
`re Councillor` MEANS `a Councillor`
`re FPA` MEANS `a member of the First Peoples' Assembly`
`re 14f` MEANS `an Examiner, an Ombudsman officer, a VAGO officer, a Judicial Commission officer, or the Parliamentary Workplace Standards and Integrity Commission or its people`
`re 14g` MEANS `the Chief Commissioner of Police or another office holder listed in s 14(g)`
`re MLA` MEANS `a member of the Legislative Assembly, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary`
`re MLC` MEANS `a member of the Legislative Council, including as a Minister or Parliamentary Secretary`
`re Minister` MEANS `a Minister who is not a member of Parliament`
`re PSB` MEANS `a public service body or its members, officers or employees`
`re Council` MEANS `a Council or its officers or employees`
`re GW` MEANS `Gellung Warl, its staff, or a Nyerna Yoorrook Telkuna or Nginma Ngainga Wara member`
`re GW CEO` MEANS `the Chief Executive Officer of Gellung Warl`
`re PPO` MEANS `an employee, delegate or agent of a prescribed public officer`
`re anyone` MEANS `any other person or body`

`improper` MEANS `improper conduct by a person, public officer or public body`
`reprisal` MEANS `detrimental action by a public officer or public body in reprisal for a public interest disclosure`
`shows` MEANS `the information shows or tends to show it`
`believe` MEANS `I reasonably believe the information shows or tends to show it`

`harassment` MEANS `intimidation or harassment`
`injury` MEANS `action causing injury, loss or damage`
`employment` MEANS `discrimination, disadvantage or adverse treatment in my employment, career, profession, trade or business, including discipline`
`other action` MEANS `some other action`

`to IBAC` MEANS `made to the IBAC under Division 2 of Part 2`
`via s 21` MEANS `made to another entity that must notify it for assessment under s 21(2)`
`not assessable` MEANS `none of these, so not an assessable disclosure`

§§ `Dates`

-- 28 days after 15 January 2027 is 12 February 2027 (16 days to 31 January, 12 in February); 28 days after 10 February
-- 2028 is 9 March 2028 (2028 is a leap year: 19 days to 29 February, 9 in March); 6 months after 31 August 2027 is 29
-- February 2028 (no 31st: last day, fork F1); 12 months after 29 February 2028 is 28 February 2029; 30 days after 1
-- February 2028 is 2 March 2028; 30 days after 1 March 2027 is 31 March 2027.
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 15 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 12 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 28 `days after` (`d` 10 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 9 3 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 30 `days after` (`d` 1 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 2 3 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 30 `days after` (`d` 1 3 2027) EQUALS `d` 31 3 2027

